{
  "name": "Household Ledger - Check-In Reply Listener (SCAFFOLD, not deployed)",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## SCAFFOLD \u2014 NOT DEPLOYED\nCompanion to Household_Ledger_CheckIn_Agent.json \u2014 must run 24/7 alongside it, same as how BNS's Telegram Approval Listener runs alongside its main content workflow. Node shape below is a direct adaptation of beautifulnaturescenes-/beautiful_naturescenes_telegram_approval_listener_workflow.json (read directly to reuse the real pattern rather than inventing a new one) \u2014 swapped from YES/NO parsing to the LOW:/FINISHED: list format the Check-In Agent's message asks for.\n\nSETUP TODOs:\n1. Connect the same Telegram bot credential as the Check-In Agent (Open Decision #3 \u2014 same bot as BNS's Approval bot, or a separate household one?).\n2. Connect a Google Sheets credential + real spreadsheet ID.\n3. Replace the chat-ID filter with the real household chat.\n\nHOW IT WORKS: fires on every message to the bot, filters to the household chat, parses LOW:/FINISHED:/NONE replies, reads Settings for a pending CheckIn_ResumeURL, and POSTs the parsed lists to that URL \u2014 waking the paused Check-In Agent execution.",
        "height": 480,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "note-1",
      "name": "Setup Notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        -420
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "updates": [
          "message"
        ]
      },
      "id": "telegram-trigger",
      "name": "Listen for Check-In Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegramTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        -1000,
        100
      ],
      "notes": "Fires on every message to the bot, from anyone. The next node filters to the household chat ID only."
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.message.chat.id }}",
              "rightValue": "REPLACE_WITH_TELEGRAM_CHAT_ID",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "if-correct-chat",
      "name": "From Household Chat?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -780,
        100
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "noop-wrong-chat",
      "name": "Ignore - Wrong Chat",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.noOp",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        220
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Parses 'LOW: item, item' / 'FINISHED: item, item' / 'NONE' replies.\n// Same normalize-then-validate shape as BNS's Parse Reply node, adapted from a single\n// YES/NO check to two labeled comma-separated lists.\nconst msg = $input.first().json.message;\nconst text = (msg.text || '').trim();\nconst chatId = msg.chat.id;\n\nif (/^none$/i.test(text)) {\n  return [{ json: { chatId, isValidReply: true, lowItems: [], finishedItems: [] } }];\n}\n\nconst lowMatch = text.match(/LOW:\\s*(.+?)(?:\\n|$)/i);\nconst finishedMatch = text.match(/FINISHED:\\s*(.+?)(?:\\n|$)/i);\nconst splitList = (m) => (m ? m[1].split(',').map(s => s.trim()).filter(Boolean) : []);\n\nconst lowItems = splitList(lowMatch);\nconst finishedItems = splitList(finishedMatch);\nconst isValidReply = Boolean(lowMatch || finishedMatch);\n\nreturn [{ json: { chatId, isValidReply, lowItems, finishedItems } }];"
      },
      "id": "code-parse-reply",
      "name": "Parse Reply",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        -560,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose"
          },
          "conditions": [
            {
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.isValidReply }}",
              "rightValue": true,
              "operator": {
                "type": "boolean",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      },
      "id": "if-valid-reply",
      "name": "Valid Format?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        -340,
        0
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "chatId": "={{ $json.chatId }}",
        "operation": "sendMessage",
        "text": "Reply with LOW: item, item / FINISHED: item, item (either line optional), or NONE if nothing changed."
      },
      "id": "telegram-nudge",
      "name": "Nudge - Invalid Format",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.telegram",
      "typeVersion": 1.2,
      "position": [
        -120,
        140
      ]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "documentId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "1sPxqWNLfs5bT7hSJBgjwTdwJVx7l01D9VQXmKNB5-5Y",
          "mode": "id"
        },
        "sheetName": {
          "__rl": true,
